## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

❌ **Never Do:**
- Use `var` or mutable collections
- Throw exceptions instead of using error types
- Block operations without proper effect types
- Hardcode configuration values
- Log sensitive trading information
- Deep recursion without trampolining
- Ignore compiler warnings about effects

✅ **Always Do:**
- Handle all side effects through IO
- Use immutable data structures
- Validate all external inputs
- Clean up resources properly
- Test algorithmic properties
- Document complex recursion schemes
- Use types to prevent invalid states

